  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IDAHOBIT 2025 : Putting a human (rights) face to LGBTIQ+ forcibly displaced persons in South Africa. &#x2018;Seeking Safety, Upholding Dignity&apos;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is an IDAHOBIT commemorative event cohosted with the Fruit Basket, UN OHCHR, UNHCR  and  the embassy of Ireland which will take place on 19 May 2025. The event will launch a  photo exhibition titled &#x201c;Putting a human (rights) face to LGBTIQ+ forcibly displaced persons in South Africa&#x201d;. This will be followed by a panel discussion.
 
The initiative aims to celebrate and amplify the voices of persons who have been forcibly displaced on the basis of discrimination and violence they face as a result of their sexual orientation, gender identity, expression, or sex characteristics. 

The exhibition will reflect on the complexity of the lives of LGBTQI+ forcibly displaced persons and communities in South Africa - highlighting accomplishments, challenges, community, and hope. The event will bring together LGBTIQ+ migrants, human rights defenders, development partners, policy makers, academics and allies. The opening to the public for a month for free.</narrative>
  </description>
